Z||000009||SteveJ||08-11-2001||08:04 AM||||Over the years I have seen several of those OEM jacks collapse. Sometimes it is the screw and nut. Other times The roll pin used to hold the hex drive nut on the end. Mercifully I think they have stopped the roll pin construction but no telling what other manufacturers are doing.<P>ANYBODY THAT DOESN'T USE JACK STANDS <B>IS NUTS!</B><P>. . .and if you don't have 'em at least put a wheel with a mounted tire under the side rail so you limit the amount you will be crushed to a survivable amount.||||reg||1
Z||000010||deceler8||08-11-2001||09:46 AM||||I would check the boneyards for a jack from a GM intermediate or full-size car. The last one I used (from a Bonneville) looked similar to the Fiero jack, but I have no idea whether it will fit in the stock space under the hood.||||reg||1
